                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aa36de93-0d02-310b-b692-2463e027ee41",
                        "entry_id": "4fac816b-b70c-3240-8f93-5539c53e365b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Without a (living) mother."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1074ae0b-6528-4f30-bf7c-018f2cc376fe",
                                "sense_id": "aa36de93-0d02-310b-b692-2463e027ee41",
                                "text": "Of 110 boys, all very far below the average in physique, forty-four had a mother at home, but sixty-six were all practically motherless. In some cases the mother was dead, but in the rest the mother was absent all day at work."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f7ee5866-0502-3d2f-a8f1-bcb784961c80",
                        "entry_id": "4fac816b-b70c-3240-8f93-5539c53e365b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Without mother (mucilaginous substance in fermenting liquid)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb8fb9d1-3af8-4b90-a844-7cad684ae97d",
                                "sense_id": "f7ee5866-0502-3d2f-a8f1-bcb784961c80",
                                "text": "Your onely way to make a good pomander, is this. Take an ownce of the pureſt garden mould, clenſed and ſteeped ſeauen daies in change of motherleſſe roſe water, then take the beſt Labdanum, Benioine, both Storaxes, amber greece, and Ciuet, and muſke, incorporate them together, and work them into what form you pleaſe; this, if your breath bee not to valiant, will make you ſmell as ſweete as my Ladies dogge."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "efc168d6-b5b5-4a3f-933b-3025abe8834a",
                                "sense_id": "f7ee5866-0502-3d2f-a8f1-bcb784961c80",
                                "text": "Once the bottle is opened, the starter may develop again if the vinegar is in your cupboard for awhile.^([sic]) If its appearance bothers you, strain the vinegar through several layers of cheesecloth into a sterilized bottle. Motherless or not, vinegar has [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "45e57cb5-04ae-4657-ab24-331e13bdba32",
                                "sense_id": "f7ee5866-0502-3d2f-a8f1-bcb784961c80",
                                "text": "A number of things along the way, such as temperature fluctuations, bacteria, and dust in the air, can derail and ruin a motherless vinegar. But if you use a mother, [...]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "96971d72-f880-3deb-a541-69186476932e",
                        "entry_id": "4fac816b-b70c-3240-8f93-5539c53e365b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Without a history or predecessor."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "18c0d66d-02b6-4ef2-9e72-7682bcb6f71f",
                                "sense_id": "96971d72-f880-3deb-a541-69186476932e",
                                "text": "Although there had been some previous attempts in the same direction, Boole's idea by no means grew from what other men had conceived, but, as truly as any mental product may, sprang from the brain of genius, motherless."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b913d35-365c-41f5-9b26-27dd8fc101e1",
                                "sense_id": "96971d72-f880-3deb-a541-69186476932e",
                                "text": "So in an inclusive act of recognition, here's our goopy take on this motherless dish—a mash-up of all your food-court chickens, be they sweet 'n' sour, sesame[.]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
